    "name": "E2E HubSpot - Updated Contact Trigger",
    "type": "automation",
    "notes": {
        "d4000004-0000-4000-8000-0000000000ff": {
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption\n\n- Appmixer account: auth+hubspot@appmixer.com (service appmixer:hubspot), HubSpot portal 148964607 (developer test account).\n- The HubSpot app's webhook target URL must point at this Appmixer instance (own app: appId + apiKey in the service config) — the triggers register / re-activate their subscriptions at flow start.\n- NewContact (re-)activates the `contact.creation` subscription, so the creation-time propertyChange events are dropped — both UpdatedContact triggers must fire on the phone update only (their Asserts expect the new phone, an emission on creation fails them).\n- Two UpdatedContact triggers on purpose: both must receive the same change (the dedupe cache key is per component).\n- Cleanup deliberately runs in the provoke lane (Wait 1m → delete, wired into AfterAll), not after AfterAll: it is not known which of the two UpdatedContact lanes completes AfterAll, and AfterAll passes on only that lane's scope, so a cleanup variable from a fixed lane could be undefined.\n- The Waits must stay: subscription propagation, create → update spacing, cleanup after the triggers read the contact (~5 s after the event).",
            "x": 64,
            "y": 32,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 256
        }
